.TH ANODIZE 1 "2026-09-25" "Dots" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anodize \- author palettes and recoverable Dots themes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anodize
[presentation-options] COMMAND [options]
.br
.B dots anodize
COMMAND [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and edit palettes from local images, seed colors, existing Dots themes,
or imported palette files. Saves use recoverable file transactions.
Saving does not activate a theme; use the apply command separately.
.PP
Mutating commands prompt on interactive input. Without a terminal or with
\fB\-\-json\fR, omission of \fB\-\-yes\fR returns a preview.
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR always takes precedence over \fB\-\-yes\fR.
Read-only operations create no persistent state.
New themes use the user configuration theme directory; --builtin selects
repository themes.
promote moves a user theme into repository themes; --copy requires --name with
a new ID.
--interactive opens guided selection and draft editing. Missing terminal
inputs use selectors.
FZF previews show theme backgrounds and syntax samples; mode choices use
temporary generated palettes.
.SH PRESENTATION OPTIONS
These options precede COMMAND and use the equals form.
.TP
.B \-\-color=auto|always|never
Control human-output colors. Auto requires a terminal, a non-dumb TERM,
and no nonempty NO_COLOR. Always overrides NO_COLOR.
After create, \fB\-\-color HEX\fR instead specifies a seed color.
.TP
.B \-\-icons=auto|always|never
Control icons where supported.
.TP
.B \-\-logo=text|auto|kitty|chafa
Choose logo rendering (default: text). This Anodize option also works after
COMMAND.
Auto selects supported Kitty graphics, then optional foreground-only Chafa
braille, then bundled text.
UTF-8 braille text assets need no converter. Missing assets, ASCII-only or
redirected output use a small ASCII mark.
Disabled color retains monochrome braille. Disabled icons, dumb terminals and
non-Unicode output skip Chafa.
.TP
.B \-\-logo\-layout=auto|horizontal|stacked|icon
Choose a layout fitted to the destination width. Also accepted after COMMAND.
All text banners use the usage artwork: horizontal, stacked, then the largest
fitting numbered logo and the base symbol.
Explicit horizontal or stacked layouts try that asset before icon fallbacks.
Ordinary text banners use at most half the available height, capped at 16
rows.
Interactive and completion previews fit pane width with a 16-row artwork
budget and preserve artwork spacing. Short panes scroll vertically.
Preview capture pipes do not force ASCII. Data output is unchanged.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help without needing the engine.
